                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8b14361-a8e6-44c1-a681-396b5637fa49",
                                "sense_id": "4cfd6e69-fca1-3dfb-9a8e-75872eae5806",
                                "text": "W gnieździe siedziały trzy orlęta, wciąż głodne."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "09dc03c6-9545-365b-856a-f0b28a33f96d",
                        "entry_id": "01e1ce32-8cd7-3120-9aa3-8f1f566acde4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "młody obrońca polskiego Lwowa z lat 1918–1920"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "metaphoric"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "006230dd-8997-4584-b9d5-53252be7d7bc",
                                "sense_id": "09dc03c6-9545-365b-856a-f0b28a33f96d",
                                "text": "Do powstania legendy Orląt Lwowskich przyczyniła się także postawa harcerek i harcerzy, zarówno lwowskich, jak i z całego kraju, którzy masowo wzięli udział w obronie Lwowa i Galicji Wschodniej"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "850e6262-349d-456e-8f54-a83668e5b7c3",
                                "sense_id": "09dc03c6-9545-365b-856a-f0b28a33f96d",
                                "text": "Uchwałą Rady Miasta Katowice nr nr X/139/11 z 30 maja 2011 roku estakadzie nadano nazwę estakada Orląt Lwowskich"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f5cae4bb-fb13-4de3-84fc-d08eb1d95186",
                        "source_entry_id": "01e1ce32-8cd7-3120-9aa3-8f1f566acde4",
                        "source_sense_id": "4cfd6e69-fca1-3dfb-9a8e-75872eae5806",
                        "target_lang_word": "eaglet",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "eaglet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd88a0bf-7ecd-333b-a152-c45ec34fce95",
                                        "entry_id": "40323fbd-de4c-3341-88ae-94c04b9517a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The immature young of an eagle; an eagle chick."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9c16298-8dcd-4ea0-be03-3bd5b8133c78",
                                                "sense_id": "bd88a0bf-7ecd-333b-a152-c45ec34fce95",
                                                "text": "He [Christopher North] speaks in his \"Second Canticle\" of \"the imps,\" \"the eaglets,\" \"the young ones,\" \"the bursting of the shells,\" as though it were the commoner occurrence for there to be several eaglets in a nest. This is not the case."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19a5d3e8-5235-446a-ab05-214ef2e24b83",
                                                "sense_id": "bd88a0bf-7ecd-333b-a152-c45ec34fce95",
                                                "text": "Alas! in the morning the eaglet was gone; and, full of sorrow, they stooped to pick up the shining fleece with which the floor was spread. At their touch, every feather became a golden coin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "040658e7-267a-4e14-81c2-70329da038b0",
                                                "sense_id": "bd88a0bf-7ecd-333b-a152-c45ec34fce95",
                                                "text": "[A]fter the ten days Arkirie came to the king and asked him to give him two eaglets."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7416bdd3-2ff8-45ca-80d9-a217e009ca58",
                                                "sense_id": "bd88a0bf-7ecd-333b-a152-c45ec34fce95",
                                                "text": "Once the eaglets are born—tiny balls of white fuzz—the adult eagles prove that birds can be as protective and solicitous of their young as humans. They'll rip food into bite-size pieces for the eaglets and stand ceaseless watch over the eyrie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f767ed8-9850-4a09-86af-ad00f0dbd9a6",
                                                "sense_id": "bd88a0bf-7ecd-333b-a152-c45ec34fce95",
                                                "text": "The early days and weeks of an eaglet’s life are not without risks."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dbcb6a53-9a80-4d75-b270-51e1bbb5d893",
                        "source_entry_id": "01e1ce32-8cd7-3120-9aa3-8f1f566acde4",
                        "source_sense_id": "4cfd6e69-fca1-3dfb-9a8e-75872eae5806",
                        "target_lang_word": "aiglon",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "aiglon",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "434bd191-03ea-3f12-a807-dbb5b01c2a9e",
                                        "entry_id": "1b278b43-c79a-30ff-8727-b64d14492f98",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Le petit de l’aigle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f26efdaa-6878-408a-bf7e-477487877c41",
                                                "sense_id": "434bd191-03ea-3f12-a807-dbb5b01c2a9e",
                                                "text": "Une aigle avec ses aiglons dans son aire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6d4aaa6-7bc0-41c9-aeff-6dd524d40785",
                                                "sense_id": "434bd191-03ea-3f12-a807-dbb5b01c2a9e",
                                                "text": "Un jeune aiglon."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6cb7600-0fa7-41ff-b0a1-22e57615790a",
                                                "sense_id": "434bd191-03ea-3f12-a807-dbb5b01c2a9e",
                                                "text": "Philippe.– Depuis quand le vieil aigle reste-t-il dans le nid, quand ses aiglons vont à la curée ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a860596-7a6d-473a-bdd0-f32347dfc6f5",
                                                "sense_id": "434bd191-03ea-3f12-a807-dbb5b01c2a9e",
                                                "text": "Un aiglon l’occupe, mais il est difficile d’estimer sa taille et son âge."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7072563e-6b4d-3466-a341-ae7dfdfa6e00",
                                        "entry_id": "1b278b43-c79a-30ff-8727-b64d14492f98",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Modèle de coiffure. Voir aussi coiffure à l’Aiglon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
